Z||000012||DRH||09-14-2001||02:43 PM||||I would argue that the religion is simply a tool being used by power hungry MEN to help manipulate the population. The Koran teaches peace. These men take a few statements in it and twist it to futher their own causes.<P>The people in that region are being told the reason their life is miserable is because Allah is angry with them for letting us defile his world. Everytime we bomb them yet leave the people in power there, we are just making it worse.<P>This is exactly why what we did 10 years ago in Iraq was so STUPID. Hussein is blaming us for their misery. We bomb the crap out of them, make them MORE miserable, then leave him there to continue blaming us. All we did was reinforce his power inside Iraq!!!<P>We have to quit making these stupid assumptions that "those people" are somehow inferior and incapable of rational thought. Yes there are a few mad men out there. But when a whole population seems to be mad it must be because they either are being manipulated by a mad man or we are somehow missing something...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||09-14-2001||02:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Tonker: Nope, he's being serious..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Sigh.. No offense to some poeple here, but learn how war works before jumping to conclusions such as flattening an entire country, etc..  You people still think the US is invincible, while it just suffered the worst terrorist attack ever. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>First JohnnyK, You need to go to your local library and check out some history books. Although the recent terrorist attack is the worst one, That doesn't mean we lost the battle. They struck first. Yes it was a devistating attack. Once the terrorist group is confirmed I highly doubt they will have a chance to do much of anything except run. (but they can't far enough!)<BR>Just so you know, Pearl Harbor was the worst attack on the U.S. prior to the recent attack. Being out numbered 2 to 1 by an experienced Navy, we still turned them back. It had nothing to do with being "invincible" It had to to with Determination, Pride, and Patriotism.<P>The terrorists thought that after the attack we would cower from them. They are wrong. In fact going thru the history books, No country that had it's citizens attacked ever backed down or cowered. Bombing and/or attacking civilians has always increased the determination and motivation of the military to defeat the enemies. Many different countries have proven this time and again.<BR>You also must understand that prior to the recent attacks, Terrorists acts were treated as "incidents" from a political point of view. The latest one is not an incident but an act of war. Now think about this, Once the culprits have been identified and located, The U.S. military <B>AND</B> all the allied countries will attack, capture, and/or eliminate them. We have public agreements with all the NATO nations, Russia, and Pakastan. I don't care how big these terrorists think they are. When the top 75% of the countries on this planet are against you there is no place to run or hide. The benefits of eliminating the terrorist organization is shared by ALL nations. <BR>These may not be the last acts of war the terrorists do, But when it's all over The world will be a safer place for all the countries.<P> Why does everyone think the U.S. is in this alone? Even China is ticked because they had business offices in the WTC too. There was a reason it was called the "World" Trade Center. The terrorists took it out thinking it was only a U.S. symbol. It was a Symbol for the world. So we could bring nations and countries together into a world market. The terrorists don't like that. When countires are divided their terror is more effective. When countries unite together terrorism weakens. I think they are beginning to realize the huge mistake they made. If they had just hit the Pentagon, They would just have to deal with the wrath of the U.S. Now they have 75% of the world against them. Considering 2/3 of the planet is water and 75% of the countries are looking for you, That leaves a very small piece of real estate to hide in.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000014||My7Fieros||09-14-2001||03:29 PM||||Im gonna take a <B>big</B> step here and say I actually agree for the most part w/Ed. Dont get me wrong, but you really do need to think about what he just said. (I never thought Id hear myself say this.)<BR>Sigh, I dont know, its really hard to put into perspective. Terrorism needs to be completely eliminated. These people serve absolutly <B>NO</B> usefullness in the world...nothing positive at least. Dont preach to me about "being on their level" or anything like that. Terrorist are a MAJOR threat to the rest of the entire world. <BR>If Russia, China, and most every other nation in the world is standing strong behind us, then its time to take action. No hate speaches here, simply stating the facts.<BR>Im <B>NOT</B> talking about genocide, Im talking about doing away w/ terrorists, and, like GWB said, all that support them. Im sorry if this offends some of you, but times..they are a changing now..............<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tonker||09-14-2001||04:02 PM||||Nobody is denying that we need to do away with terrorists. The terrorists have declared war on us, and we will respond. What I disagree with is the hateful vitriol being spewed out against all Arabs since this incident occurred. Here is what it all boils down to:<P><B>Racism is racism no matter what group you target. Genocide is genocide no matter what group you exterminate.</B> It would be no different than saying that the Jews serve no purpose and they should be exterminated. We've heard that before and it's no less wrong in the case of the Arabs.<P>Yes, some Arabs engage in and support terrorism. At the same time there are Americans, Canadians, Irish, Israelis and Germans who do the same thing. You wouldn't suggest that we do away with all people of Irish stock and heritage based on the actions of the IRA or ULF. I see no difference in the case of the Arabs. <P>If you believe what Eds tells you, then I'm going to suggest that it is time to educate yourself. Forming your opinions on the basis arguments presented by either myself or Eds, that are for the most part not supported by factual evidence is very dangerous. We are not - I believe, though I can only speak for myself - experts in this field. I have some educational background, but not enough to be able to speak in a particularly intelligent or articulate fashion about this. We are people with our own opinions. I believe that Eds is wrong, he seems to think the same about me. To base your own opinions on ours is just to compound our errors. If you want to make your own determination about arab culture, meet with some, learn about the Koran, take some University (college, I believe you call it) level courses on Middle Eastern politics and history. Don't base your assumptions on ours, though.<P>To me, it doesn't matter how you explain it or describe it. No matter what justification you use, the fact remains that annihilating a "race" of people is still genocide. It's as wrong today as it was when the Nazis did it. To hear people suggest this, means to me that we have forgotten the hard-learned lessons of our past. Some rules never change.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||13
