Z||000041||87GTZ34||09-15-2001||11:05 AM||||Huh - I think Ed planted his own type of bomb (post) and ran...<P>A couple of points:<P>  First of all, out gov't will never ever practice extermination it is against international law.  Also, it may be totally ineffective, as unless they identify the proper target, they won't hit the proper target.<P>Also to say all Muslim & Arabs is evil is false.  I have witnessed for myself as I have Arab friends (both Christian & Muslims) as well as Muslims from other origins.  Most are U.S. citizens and one of them is a U.S. Army vet of the Gulf war and a tank pilot or driver whatever they're called.  There are actually a small percentage of terrorists when compared to all Arabs or Muslims (not the same group by the way).  Only terrorist act out violently with real weapons (more than rock throwing).  The rest as someone has mentioned have been conditioned that the U.S. is the reason behind their misery (mainly by support of the Israel).<P>The U.S. has also harbored a form of terrorist in the past and a much larger org than Tim McVeigh.  The KKK by definition is 'an organization that uses a systematic means of violence, terror and intimidation to achieve an end.  While we worked on reducing their impact, we didn't try to eradicate them.<P>Our gov't has called this an act of war (which I agree with).  It is not the first though as U.S. planes have been bombed out of the sky and U.S. embassies have been destroyed by suicide bombers in the past (to name a few).  Our Administration at the time decided to make an example out of a few people that would die for their cause and throw them in prison as a deterrent.  This would leave the 'army' intact to fight (in a cowardly manner) another day and take more U.S. lives.  Each 'battle' escalates into a larger next battle (more lives lost & more destruction).  Hopefully our current administration has what it takes (nerve) and backing from the rest of our gov't and other govt's to eradicate or drastically reduce terrorism from ALL origins.  So Ed's original 'get a flame going statement' is nonsense.<P>I only hope that this exercise can start soon enough and be effective enough that we can have a fun and exciting winter olympics in Feb.<P>Peace<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000042||rogergarrison||09-15-2001||05:09 PM||||Im Not against anyone, muslim, arab, afghani, mexican, irish or anything else when there legalized americans here. There all American by changing their citizenship. Im not against them staying in their own countries and running them anyway they see fit-as long as it dont affect me. BUT-when a country OR that countries government supports this type of thing -be it Sadam, Bin Ladin or anyony else, ALL the people accept the responsibilites or consequences that they get. If it takes wiping out 3/4 of Afghanistan to get the message across to anyone else, I feel so be it. They have all become too accustomed to knowing we just blow it off. The reason we lost in Viet Nam was because we were only allowed to attack military targets. I know because I flew 100 missions there. We were not allowed to attack anything close to for example schools, hospitals, residential areas. It didnt take too long for them to figure out to just park their tanks and missiles there and we would wouldnt touch them. If we had been given the chance to attack them wherever they were, there would be no North Viet Nam. Like I said in another post, we were not limited like that in WWII, we bombed Dresden Germany into oblivion as well as Hamburg, Berlin. Thats how we won. Not only shooting at guys in black or green uniforms. Japan was the same, Hiroshima and Nagasaki, were the same. We erased them-and they surrendered. Now we have to go after the terrorists all the same way-their being protected and its time for the protectors to pay.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 09-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000043||EdsB52||09-16-2001||03:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>Stop being an idiot Eds. You seem to be intelligent for the most part. Start showing it.<P>You know what? If we were to go by your logic, Christians would have been exterminated long ago. The Crusades were not about being a kind and loving people.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stop being a pacifist, Tonker. You are from a neutral nation; you don't understand the politics of the US from other than a third party perspective, as well as you have nothing at stake. Christians were exterminated; have you forgotten about Rome in the B'C. Era? I'm not advocating that as a positive event, just reiterating history. And actually no, my logic does not prescribe that Christians be exterminated. Absent aberrations, Christians don't subscribe to extermination or murder as a way of forcing people to believe as they do; they use legislation, which is a rational avenue. Still coercive, but rational. The reason for a sudden change of my attitude is that when you cross a certain line where rational, constructive negotiations are beyond reach, you need to equal or exceed the force received. I love to hear cogent arguments from formidable opponents and tend to lean toward the liberal side and give the benefit of the doubt to the weaker side, but when that line is crossed all bets are off; you need to cease negotiations. Like maryjane wrote, negotiations are for losers.||||reg||1
Z||000044||EdsB52||09-16-2001||03:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>Ed you just sound like a compleat MORON.<P>Learn something, anything about the Muslim religion before you open your mouth with this crap again.<P>and just fo the record Muslim is spelt with one S not two<P>[This message has been edited by Neal (edited 09-14-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What a coincidence, Neal and bob's moniker block reads, "Neal<BR>Member <BR>Posts: 117<BR>From:Calgary AB, Canada"<P>Again, not to include all Canadians, as there are some men up there and I think I can speak for most Americans by saying we're proud to have you as neighbors.<P>I realize Muslim is spelled with 1 ‘s.’ If you read the thread you’ll see that all Muslim words possess 1 ‘s,’ I just didn’t proofread the title. Remember, you started the spelling bee here. But since we’re here, look at the quality of the literacy in your 6-word post. You started a sentence with a lowercase ‘a,’ forgot the ‘r’ in for, and spelled ‘complete’ as “compleat.” Learn something about being a man before you attempt to tell the toughest country in the world how to run their defense/offense. Don’t worry, we won’t ask your tampon-wearing ass to help out. Why don’t you go to Mach 10’s house and exchange fashion and makeup secrets?||||reg||1
