Z||000046||EdsB52||09-16-2001||03:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Tonker: Nope, he's being serious..  :( Sigh.. No offense to some poeple here, but learn how war works before jumping to conclusions such as flattening an entire country, etc..  You people still think the US is invincible, while it just suffered the worst terrorist attack ever. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Johnny, my friend, WE ARE INVINCIBLE. How old are you Johnny? I believe you are fairly young, while addressing people much older. I don't mean to pull age-rank on you, as I view you as intelligent. But what I'm trying to convey is that you're asking Viet Nam veterans (for which I'm not one of) to learn something about war. I have worked on war machines all of my life, including a hitch in AF with overseas duty. I've been around war and war machines, and have done much studying about various wars, so I feel fairly qualified to understand it. Oh, in case you forgot, WE ARE INVINCILBLE. ||||reg||1
