Z||000053||EdsB52||09-16-2001||05:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>MJ,<P>The Usual Niceties:<BR>First of all I have to disagree with one point. My first responsibility isn't to the men, it's to the mission. The mission, the men, then you. Everything else comes dead last. There are some cases where I would violate this rule, but you can't worry about losing lives at the expense of you objective, otherwise you might as well not be there at all.<P>The problem were having is that we're looking at this from two different levels. Rather than answer this question directly I'm going to tell you how I would handle things from both perspectives. Here is how I would assuage my bleeding heart conscience.<P>At the strategic level:<BR>1) Once it's determined who we are really looking for - let's be honest Bin-Ladin should be on the list regardless of whether he planned and organised this attack. He was found responsible for a previous attack and is an on-going security risk - and where the individuals are hiding, you tell the appropriate government that they will immediately hand his ass over or face the consequences of a war against the international coalition arrayed against them. If they hand him over, great, look at how many lives you've just saved.<P>2) If they refuse, you inform them that there now exists a state of war. The country will be informed that any opposition will be considered to be an enemy force. Any civillian center found harbouring the terrorist will also be considered to be an enemy force. All enemy forces will be eliminated. You've just given them the chance to save their own people. If they refuse, the blood is now on their hands.<P>3)The use of missiles and airstrikes on strategic targets can be used to indicate that we are serious.<P>4) The troops go in and start kicking ass. Where possible, the population should be informed to remain in their homes for the duration of hostilities to reduce unnecessary casualties.<P>Tactical:<BR>5) When my platoon and I get to this village, their government and the people have been informed about the consequences of harboring terrorists. I know that my government and superiors have taken every possible opportunity to to save innocent lives. That being said the lives of my men are my priority and responsibility. This is where I call in the air-strike and let God sort 'em out. This, of course, depends on my mission. If my superiors want this guy alive reducing the building to rubble isn't going to accomplish it, is it?<P>Let me point out that I do not begin with the assumption that all the "rag-heads" deserve to die. Where possible I try to avoid civillian casualties. Despite this I'm not going to allow my men to be slaughtered just to save these people. This is what I meant by proceeding judiciously. <P>The Real Issue:<BR>That fact remains that this thread is dedicated to the argument that Islamics are evil and deserve to die. Also that "America has always borne the burden of acting more " 'human' that(sic) other nations" and that Islamics should be exterminated "regardless of humanity restraints" because they "want to exterminate us". I argue that, this argument is absolutely without merit. It is based on the incorrect premise that Muslims as a whole want to destroy us. This is simply not the case. It is not part of their religion, it is not part of their nature. It is instead a small disenfranchised group no different than terrorist groups we have seen in western culture. The fact that this group invokes their religion in attempt to justify their actions does not mean that it is actually part of their religion. Christians rode into the Middle East in the dark ages, slaughtering Muslims and Jews (and each other)  in their zealousness to recover Jerusalem in the name of the Church. This is hardly indicative of 'typical' Christian values is it?<P>Also, at no point are we absolved of our requirement to act humanely. It is for this very reason that the Geneva Conventions were established. Humanity in warfare - as unlikely as it seems - is just as important as humanity in peace time. The fact the the Nazis and the Japanese violated the Geneva Conventions did not stop the Allies from treating German prisoners of war as was required by the Convention during WW2. Instead it steeled our resolve to punish those who violated these rules. Nuremburg was not about retribution or revenge, it was about teaching us about the costs of forgetting our humanity.<P>I have never  argued that we must avoid civilian casualties at all costs. I have argued that we have a responsibility to behave towards others as we would have others behave towards us if the situations were reversed. I don't say this because of any religious or cultural belief, but instead because I know it to be right. From what I've read others apparently know it to be right as well. I'm hoping the rest of the people are simply showing a natural human reaction to pain and/or fear. I want to find the people who caused this atrocious act, I want them to be punished in what ever manner is fitting and I want to make damn sure this never happens again. I don't believe that genocide is the way to do this. <P>MJ, I've tried to answer your question as openly and completely as I can. Now I have a question, not only for you but for everyone else who reads this. It is basically the distilled issue of this thread, as I understand it after having read Eds' initial post. It is a fairly straightforward one and one that people seem to keep skirting about. Is it acceptable to eradicate an entire race of people as Eds is suggesting?  Not is it acceptable to kill civilians or should the lives of our troops have priority or should we punish terrorists. I have presented my position and arguments already. [b]Is <I>genocide</I> acceptable to you, yes or no?</B><P>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 09-15-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wrote:<P>"My answer parallels GW's sentiments; the war has changed and the rules have changed, so we must change with them. If we need to exterminate an entire race of people that want to exterminate us, then we should, regardless of humanity restraints. America has always borne the burden of acting more "human" that other nations and I'm sick of that requirement."<P>Tonker wrote:<P>"Also that "America has always borne the burden of acting more " 'human' that(sic) other nations" and that Islamics should be exterminated "regardless of humanity restraints" because they "want to exterminate us"."<P>Tonker, you just violated one of the sacred rules of English even worse than plagiarism; you misquoted me. For that I think you are a huge dick-face. Why the name-calling? When someone stoops to misquote, then are beyond rational conversation, so fnck it. You are desperate. Why else would you resort to misquoting me? To be specific, look at the part of my post where I wrote, "If we need to exterminate an entire race of people that want to exterminate us, then we should, regardless of humanity restraints." You perverted it to read, "If we need to exterminate an entire race of people...." Where in your rendition of my post does it read 'if we need to?' No, you contorted my post to fit your needs of making me out as an annihilist. You are a puke. A real journalist is supposed to post others statements in full, especially if they're trying to refute them. You simply cut and pasted my statement out of order, while using quotation marks. I don't think we should annihilate the entire race, unless necessary. If necessary, let's party. The operative word of 'necessary' is removed from your rendition of my post, and refutes your inference (in my perception) of me being a supporter of recreational killing. If necessary, I believe we, as Americans should destroy as many nations as we need to, to achieve survival. Don't get your nose stuck too far into a bible and forget about Darwin. Darwin and Mother Nature always win. Hopefully, and realistically, we would never need to annihilate any nation, culture, or religion.<P>"Humanity in warfare - as unlikely as it seems - is just as important as humanity in peace time."<P>Maryjane, will you beatch-slap this irritant? The problem here is that Tonker has been reading too many books. I doubt Tonker has been in any real pressure situation where no time is available to research the right decision.<P>"Is it acceptable to eradicate an entire race of people as Eds is suggesting?  Not is it acceptable to kill civilians or should the lives of our troops have priority or should we punish terrorists. I have presented my position and arguments already. [b]Is <I>genocide</I> acceptable to you, yes or no?"<P>No anus, Eds is not suggesting that, or at least as a first measure; if necessary. I'm so sorry, I know the "If necessary" doesn't fit into your argument so you conveniently omitted it, but it changes the entire stated desire of my post. I guess you're saying nor is it acceptable to kill civilians? What does your book say about a 5-year-old rag head running at you with a bomb strapped to his or her back? Since you have the luxury of sitting at home deciding how to handle this, try to factor in the element of 50 yards, 40 yards, 30 yards, 20 yards, 10 yards, DEAD!!! That was the distance of closure that you had to think of what to do, how did you survive? Did your conscious win or did you survive? Oh, I get it, that would never happen.||||reg||1
Z||000054||EdsB52||09-16-2001||05:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>Huh - I think Ed planted his own type of bomb (post) and ran...<P>So Ed's original 'get a flame going statement' is nonsense.<P>I only hope that this exercise can start soon enough and be effective enough that we can have a fun and exciting winter olympics in Feb.<P>Peace</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't run, boy. Because the forum was closed and we had visitors from out of town and couldn't post, you think I ran? You are a punk. When have you known me to run from an issue? Your last statement summarizes your intentions; I hope we have a fun and exciting winter Olympics. Do you realize what an asinine statement that was? Have you even heard of terrorists creating havoc at Olympic games, including many murders? Can the thousands of family members of the recently deceased, or the world have a good little time at the Olympics knowing their family member are dead and/or are at risk and the US is doing little about it? You stepped in it hard this time jackass.||||reg||1
Z||000055||TRiAD||09-16-2001||10:43 AM||||I haven't read this whole thread, so I apologize if I repeat someone. <P>There's been a statement here that Muslims follow the Koran, which teaches peace, and that there are simply some wayward splinter groups that are hateful and destructive. <P>This is true, to an extent. The Koran teaches peace, but only to other Muslims. It teaches that ALL religions except Islam are an abomination, and need to be wiped out. Mohammed taught that Christianity was polytheism, since we believe that Christ is God's Son. He says that's idolatry, and all people who don't follow Islam need to be turned to Islam, forcefully if necessary. <P>There was a Muslim holy man on TV last night saying to Christians "We both worship the same God (allah), and we bothe follow the same Prophets (Moses, Jesus, Mohammed)". He said we should band together. <P>Funny, the Jehova's Witnesses that came to my door last month used the same tactic. They, too believe Christianity is polytheism, and think we're all going to hell. But they said "we both read the Bible, we're no different than you". <P>I've got news for Muslims. Mohammed was NOT a Prophet of God, and Jesus IS God's Son. We do NOT worship the same God, because allah has no Son, there is no redemption by Grace in Islam, only by works. Jesus' death on the cross is meaningless in the eyes of Muslims. <P>In this war; we should band together with all other Americans, including Muslims; as well as with all other nations wanting to support this cause, but<BR>TO BAND TOGETHER WITH MUSLIMS ON A RELIGIOUS LEVEL IS IDOLATRY.<P>Our belief is that we should spread the Good News; peacefully. A religion that seeks to overthrow the world; forcefully if necessary, has no place in God's plan. <P><BR>I'm not saying we should wipe Muslims from the earth (unless it's by miraculous conversion of all of Islam  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), or what have you, just don't be decieved into believing that they and Christians can band together on a spiritual plane. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
